{"step_index":596,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:38:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T12:08:26+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T12:08:32+05:30\nThe search for \"\"Qwen 3.5\" OR \"Qwen3.5\" benchmarks release\" returned the following summary:\nThe **Qwen 3.5** model family was officially released by Alibaba’s Qwen team on **February 16, 2026**[1][2].\n\n### Release Overview\nThe Qwen 3.5 series was rolled out in stages to provide a range of model sizes optimized for different hardware and use cases[2]:\n\n*   **Flagship Release (February 16, 2026):** The headline model, **Qwen3.5-397B-A17B**, was released as a native vision-language model featuring a sparse Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture[3][2].\n*   **Medium Series (February 24, 2026):** Included **Qwen3.5-27B** (a dense model) alongside **Qwen3.5-35B-A3B** and **Qwen3.5-122B-A10B**[2][4].\n*   **Small Series (March 2, 2026):** Included compact models—**0.8B, 2B, 4B, and 9B**—designed for on-device efficiency[2][5].\n\n### Benchmarks and Performance\nQwen 3.5 models are noted for their native multimodal capabilities, agentic workflows, and support for a 256K–262K token context window[6][2][7][8]. Key performance highlights reported at the time include:\n\n*   **Instruction Following:** The models demonstrated strong performance on benchmarks such as **IFBench** (scoring 76.5)[3][2].\n*   **Reasoning:** The flagship model achieved competitive scores on benchmarks like **AIME 2026** (91.3) and **SWE-bench Verified** (76.4)[2][7].\n*   **Multimodal Capabilities:** Because text and image understanding were integrated at the pretraining stage, the models excel in tasks such as OCR, chart interpretation, and UI element recognition[1][5].\n\nDetailed benchmark comparisons against other frontier models (such as GPT-5.2 and Claude Opus 4.6) and information on running these models locally can be found on the [official Qwen blog](https://qwen.ai/blog) and the [Qwen Hugging Face organization page](https://huggingface.co/Qwen)[3][9].\n\nSources:\n[1] [thesys.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF3kbZ2MZVAI_hHH2O43FtJaPnSW5Zplnspn_OmI6R073P7EKYlFRdbOGPXgXwM4SmyMvsXHy2I_c1G8mbhkUz37FNZ3fbJ90rjzH-YF9m-j0_9iuay8c2vJU6s)\n[2] [substack.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG0HO1Lv4pNLp8KTD1RmQy7o0oSTOcgSZR1jwdQP5IBKUhA_9JjF8NlHKVzVrSuGxQZJnDIsDYWUJqsynR0tvGttfCIMqaoMgFCdlFAH0nT-TZXt-PgdIMOqNz-vpUFmIcdRGS1xwkaYRwq_UvP3sdG2bKd5v6f2bdpcQ4I)\n[3] [qwen.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFWdNhCLNqk9EKrpVgJciDm7Kt1UtRe3EYheqNjtvn9brU2_scvgIIz2Dni33Ovt7Ro-isil0Wkfkzhxrwu1stp0_A8sNUgHwQjKpm6zjpN5a_cf9cx)\n[4] [digitalapplied.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEebbPj4OmQlBcvbc-lGj4PUsnOzSdklpKpVZCOJ0gb9PiR314XU9-FezOTKDg8XeoiO8vZKg-fxQYI7FPqtKMTONSRbxQypdJfAMSZo1ACB4LXp69v35LzCSZ7qGUj90L6vX0_XrGYYr7FLeb7IJz6GNLeqhjZ3gGkoT4g-nzcOPbl4rf81K3duo8OuwIOfQ==)\n[5] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEwRoNbxqxvPb5qroNnW_wQrdwhQNSiI03cjgg-PDH4My_xekrB2xBwLCWrWmNvim7d3rnv4PmsCyt2Rp0j_dRtGpDURgdY8VTR7XBthTWlpvjeT0S_J9F12Hg-I75NpOngUBAqlrpJCziiE4LtSi4KEmc6w81jU1KZvFQNLHQgntyBWmUfTfHBCgr-MVNCEs4YtKxH4v3zTFDb)\n[6] [datacamp.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHdUs9vxkUezujSh2LGdNZ2Uhz19qitJKLNA-EfRtTDAmYF6YWiOsM0Qze2ymBzOV0ip_RutoMpHBiS_-zUc-VMJWrl5rMgBs3DHMF1R9rNFQUZphEs2okUkQ1e)\n[7] [morphllm.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGcezerX9m_8RNGmeR2e-XMinevQAoEwbmaQ5pbT_hjWz6kccm08sEn94YFc_kiFdF3mKhDF2SmW4ER6dJhc4g-8Mm6wKF6FA5vIE6Q4kggl2b62z9-L3c=)\n[8] [unsloth.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHca2ZyhuqEzbARHE3uDBomY9Kti8U7ZUQhg4_ZjHvnyJB3Qo_GlHd0OhNRSS4RTHzoiCvF2KS36G2QshPbJbKEnz6d-s0M-mhm88vM4NKtfxA3Y1FUQCX5SoCxdQ==)\n[9] [huggingface.co](https://vert