{"step_index":596,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:38:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T12:08:47+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T12:08:53+05:30\nThe search for \"\"Qwen3.5\" 4B benchmarks OR \"Qwen 3.5\" OR \"Qwen2.5-Coder-3B\" benchmarks OR \"Qwen2.5-Coder-7B\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe **Qwen3.5** series, released by Alibaba Cloud in February and March 2026, represents a major leap in open-weight multimodal model performance, featuring a hybrid architecture (Gated Delta Networks combined with sparse Mixture-of-Experts) and native multimodal capabilities.\n\n### Qwen3.5 Overview & Benchmarks\nThe flagship **Qwen3.5-397B-A17B** is designed for high-efficiency, frontier-level performance, activating only 17B parameters per forward pass.\n\n*   **Key Benchmark Highlights:**\n    *   **IFEval:** 92.6\n    *   **MMLU-Pro:** 87.8\n    *   **GPQA Diamond:** 88.4\n    *   **AIME 2026:** 91.3\n*   **Small Models (0.8B, 2B, 4B, 9B):** Released in March 2026, these models are optimized for edge devices and low-compute environments.\n    *   **Qwen3.5-4B:** Recognized as the most intelligent model under 5B parameters, scoring 27 on the Intelligence Index.\n    *   **Qwen3.5-9B:** The most intelligent model under 10B parameters, scoring 32 on the Intelligence Index.\n    *   These models support a 262K context window and are licensed under Apache 2.0.\n\n### Qwen2.5-Coder Series\nThe **Qwen2.5-Coder** series (released late 2024) focuses on code generation, reasoning, and repair. It is built on the Qwen2.5 architecture and trained on over 5.5 trillion tokens of code-related data.\n\n*   **Qwen2.5-Coder-3B:** \n    *   Designed as a lightweight, efficient coding assistant.\n    *   Benchmarks show it performs strongly in code-related tasks (generation, completion, and repair) relative to its size, though it is superseded by the newer Qwen3.5 small series for general multimodal tasks.\n*   **Qwen2.5-Coder-7B:** \n    *   Known for outperforming larger models like DeepSeek-Coder-V2-Lite and CodeStral-22B at the time of its release.\n    *   It maintains competitive performance in mathematics and general language tasks alongside its specialized coding capabilities.\n\n### Comparison Summary\n| Model Series | Primary Focus | Notable Features |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Qwen3.5** | Native Multimodal, Agentic, General Purpose | MoE architecture, \"Thinking\" & \"Fast\" modes, 201 languages, 262K+ context. |\n| **Qwen2.5-Coder** | Code Generation & Reasoning | Specialized code-training, state-of-the-art performance for its era (2024). |\n\n*Note: As of September 2026, the Qwen3.5 series (and subsequent updates like Qwen3.6/3.8) is the current standard for Qwen's open-weight model family, offering significant improvements in intelligence, efficiency, and multimodal integration over the Qwen2.5-Coder series.*"}
