{"step_index":598,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:38:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T12:08:58+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T12:09:02+05:30\nThe search for \"\"Qwen3.5-4B\" benchmarks OR \"Qwen3.5\" \"4B\" MMLU HumanEval GSM8K MATH\" returned the following summary:\nQwen3.5-4B is a compact, natively multimodal foundation model from Alibaba Cloud, released in March 2026 as part of the Qwen3.5 small model series. It utilizes a hybrid architecture combining Gated Delta Networks (a form of linear attention) with sparse Mixture-of-Experts.\n\n### Key Specifications\n*   **Parameters:** 4 Billion\n*   **Architecture:** Hybrid (Gated Delta Networks + Gated Attention)\n*   **Capabilities:** Natively multimodal (text, image, and video), 201 languages supported.\n*   **Context Window:** 262,144 tokens (extensible to 1M via YaRN).\n*   **License:** Apache 2.0\n\n### Benchmark Performance\nWhile specific point-in-time scores can vary based on evaluation frameworks and post-training versions, Qwen3.5-4B has been noted for high performance relative to its size, often cited alongside other models in its class:\n\n*   **MMLU-Pro:** Reported scores around **79.1%**.\n*   **GPQA (Diamond):** Reported scores around **76.2%**.\n*   **Coding & Reasoning:** The model is designed for high-throughput tasks, with DeepInfra (providing the reasoning version) demonstrating efficient latency (0.45s TTFT) and output speeds (approx. 250 tokens/sec).\n*   **Comparison:** It is frequently compared against other small models (such as those in the Gemma or Phi series). Some community benchmarks and discussions (e.g., on Reddit/LocalLLaMA) highlight that while the model is highly efficient, users should be aware that benchmark results on hosting platforms may sometimes reflect full-precision performance rather than the specific quantized (e.g., 4-bit) versions often used locally.\n\n*Note: As of September 2026, newer models in the Qwen series (such as the Qwen3.8 series) have been released with further enhancements to agentic and omnimodal capabilities.*"}
