{"step_index":600,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T06:39:07Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T12:09:07+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T12:09:14+05:30\nThe search for \"\"Qwen2.5-Coder-3B\" HumanEval MBPP EvalPlus benchmarks\" returned the following summary:\nQwen2.5-Coder-3B is part of the Qwen2.5-Coder series, a collection of code-specific Large Language Models (LLMs)[1][2]. Below is a summary regarding its benchmark performance on HumanEval, MBPP, and EvalPlus.\n\n### Benchmark Context\n*   **Performance Variability:** Performance results for the 3B model can vary significantly depending on the evaluation framework used (e.g., official technical report results vs. community-run platforms like OpenCompass)[3][4]. \n*   **Official Metrics:** In the official Qwen2.5-Coder technical report, the 3B model is noted for significant improvements in code generation, reasoning, and fixing compared to its predecessor (CodeQwen1.5)[2]. While the flagship 32B model is frequently highlighted for achieving state-of-the-art results on **EvalPlus**, **HumanEval**, and **MBPP**[1][5], the 3B model is designed as a more lightweight, efficient alternative for developers with constrained resources[5][2].\n*   **Community Reports:** Some community evaluations have reported lower pass@1 scores (e.g., ~45.12 on HumanEval and ~30.20 on MBPP via OpenCompass) compared to the higher figures sometimes associated with the broader series in promotional documentation[3][4]. These discrepancies are common in the open-source LLM community due to differences in prompting strategies, zero-shot/few-shot settings, and execution environments[3][6].\n\n### Key Characteristics\n*   **Model Architecture:** The 3B model features approximately 3.09 billion parameters, with 36 layers and a context length of 32,768 tokens[2].\n*   **Usage:** It is highly recommended to use the **Instruct** version of this model for coding tasks, as the base model is intended for continued pre-training or fine-tuning rather than direct chat or instruction following[2].\n*   **Evaluation Environment:** When evaluating models like Qwen2.5-Coder-3B, factors such a\n<truncated 208 bytes>\ned to check the **[EvalPlus Leaderboard](https://evalplus.github.io/leaderboard.html)** directly, as it provides a standardized, rigorous evaluation platform that helps normalize results across different models[7][8].\n\nSources:\n[1] [ollama.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGnlRksiSwXhL3lUHb-355qgot63-HpFPWgKbKF4Ls-smVutHECfhytm4jFMQnSlIMElqZFxS53KtCJsz3EH107GkHF5ezaHidLn8R4o5lg1I7y7CK5x-K3_arJKeKP6lZz-YTt2ZoEPVPU)\n[2] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFdrpYrHLQG_lEKrKbyPt3WyXi62yrqi25G5LWujqz8rrCk2pqeUeW2BsoRVv-3rFQQmwx8zJE0BnYk0OG4ke7pb6zKhS6W6BZj3KfT467ukdb5Kp-bukBkuDm08JjbQNUf)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG91NRE8UTFhijm5djX7hcP1RwBp-W0gR8iQ8RKg4n-HLO0e2yBo-2UgR7TxyhKSsDstFUFbYFlfFK2sRIRGTivBX-5atwMLTVj5CuPNJBGRxWQhBWIO8Cl29D-D5yN1571vc2Tbw==)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG91NRE8UTFhijm5djX7hcP1RwBp-W0gR8iQ8RKg4n-HLO0e2yBo-2UgR7TxyhKSsDstFUFbYFlfFK2sRIRGTivBX-5atwMLTVj5CuPNJBGRxWQhBWIO8Cl29D-D5yN1571vc2Tbw==)\n[5] [github.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH09cFqhOrkQmU4BHEpBJNorsYKjRXQtcbRw5z5pDqwDZDNA21mwlN0smTbn0U9m7QMGuKha9Dh7o7ePKW3QkuK4NCPZbf0BWGKwk6yOrXBKHlCUlLEzMQGFiHB9BLkCDvPXdq8UsE4qg==)\n[6] [readthedocs.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF8m8-pzf3Ckbc0sn4XpWNCrCdS_X6y4olHAbikgRubqEENt6GRh1bN3gn7qLcE6favUDdCAcjX_AlHXoraVySsZsKnZvB7966-EWoOPq7Lb9iZJpvp9dNxOXgMblKwUA--HgbzKUMT0_x4pPqLR_pQi47OHJLtMQ==)\n[7] [github.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYeok8HKtVPqbzDL2V7KwriAPxtOvDp3Cv0nxH2a1hCRUPTNE8Z8o69nu07OYBGleYvl79qtaGnpgtRU-YTlry